# Release Candidate screenshot matrix — 10 routes x 5 breakpoints.
#
# Ignored for the same reason as `.shots/`: these are review artifacts, not
# build output, and they are deterministic — `node
# scripts/capture-release-preview.mjs` against a production server reproduces
# them exactly. The matrix is ~80 MB of PNG, which is not something to carry in
# git history for something a command regenerates in minutes.
#
# The committed screenshots are the ones in `public/work/` — those are
# *published evidence*, pinned deliberately so what we show cannot drift when a
# third-party site changes.
#
# The glob covers the per-phase copies as well: RC2 keeps the RC1 matrix as
# `release-preview-rc1/` so the before/after comparison has a before, and both
# are regenerable review artifacts rather than source.
release-preview*/

# Session Supervisor: quarantined artifacts + last-run snapshot.
# Moved here rather than deleted so a crash always has a before-picture —
# the RC6.1 recovery deleted test-results/ and had to reconstruct the
# chrome-headless-shell OOM from Windows Event Log alone.
.env-quarantine/

# Engineering Supervisor: machine-local state.
#
# Baselines, locks, caches and saved page audits. Gitignored deliberately: a
# perf baseline is a claim about *this* host — 4 cores, Intel HD 620, 7.88 GB —
# and committing it would let a faster machine's numbers silently become this
# machine's budget, turning every subsequent comparison into an artefact of
# where the number came from.
.engineering/
